Thought: The search results for the SMILES string "COC1=CC(=O)OC(=C1)/C=C/C=O" do not match the proton NMR data either. I have exhausted the list of isomers without finding a match. I will now use the HSQC NMR spectra to help identify the correct structure by correlating carbon and proton shifts.
Action: hsqc_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: The HSQC NMR spectra provide correlations between proton and carbon shifts, which can help identify the structure. The data suggests the presence of a methyl group (2.12 ppm) and aromatic protons (7.43, 7.54, 7.71, 8.02 ppm) with corresponding carbon shifts. I will now validate the SMILES string "C1=CC=C(C=C1C=O)C(=O)O" which corresponds to salicylic acid, a common compound with a similar structure.
Action: validate_smiles
Action Input: {"smiles": "C1=CC=C(C=C1C=O)C(=O)O"}
